  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "YPqGwzGnSDdV6dt2KoXQVM6B1F8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:42.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "LionGate AG carries Flowable Strategic status and describes itself as a system integrator, but its market positioning is customer-experience transformation rather than open-source conviction. The record's instruction is to verify before pitching, which makes this a flagged row rather than a scored one.\n\nThe distinction the flag protects is between a certification and a posture. Strategic tier says the firm has invested in a relationship with Flowable; it says nothing about whether the firm's architecture defaults are client-owned and open, or whether it would carry that argument into a client conversation. A CX-transformation practice typically sells journeys and front-end outcomes, where the record-keeping layer underneath is an implementation detail chosen for convenience \u2014 often a managed proprietary service.\n\nThis is the same failure mode the corpus flags in other forms: Incentro had good open-source posture but hyperscaler anchoring, and several rows carry an explicit instruction to run an OSS-portfolio screen before acting. A high partner tier is the easiest signal to acquire and the weakest predictor of posture, so it should never substitute for the screen. Provenance: Flowable Partner Finder, mined 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- LionGate AG (DE Munich) \u2014 liongate.de\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Flowable Strategic + System Integrator. CX-transformation positioning, not OSS-conviction \u2014 verify before pitching \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:42.000947Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:42.000951Z"
    }
  },
